      <div class="card-title" style="color:var(--text);"><span>Are you currently exempt from AU CGT on your shares and crypto?</span></div>
      <p style="font-size:14px; margin:0 0 0.5rem;">
        <strong>Possibly</strong> — on the facts researched for this worked example (a
        non-protected Special Category Visa, no disqualifying spouse, no AU PR/citizenship
        planned), a portfolio like this one could qualify for "temporary resident" CGT
        treatment. That means <strong>CGT event I1</strong> — the rule that deems your whole
        portfolio sold the moment you cease AU tax residency — could <strong>not apply at
        all</strong>. Meridian, Northbridge, and Crypto holdings are not Australian property,
        so as a temporary resident those gains were never in the Australian CGT net to
        begin with.
      </p>
      <p style="font-size:12.5px; color:var(--text-2); margin:0;">
        This flips the moment any of three things change: an AU citizen/PR spouse, an AU PR
        grant, or citizenship. It's also the single finding in this research most worth a
        professional second opinion for your own facts — the primary ATO source couldn't be
        reached directly during this research (see the doc for why); this rests on
        secondary sources that agree with each other, not primary confirmation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="row-2 section-gap">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title"><span>AU/NZ residency tests + DTA tie-breaker</span></div>
        <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-2); margin:0;">
          Two independent questions, not one: what ends AU tax residency (a holistic "did your
          whole life move" test, no bright line), and separately what starts NZ residency (a much
          more mechanical 183-day test — easier to trigger than to escape again, since ceasing NZ
          residency needs 325+ days absent <em>and</em> no home there). The tax treaty's tie-breaker
          resolves which country gets taxing rights if both apply at once — it does <em>not</em> by
          itself end Australian residency under Australia's own law, which is what actually
          triggers CGT event I1.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title"><span>AU CGT event I1 — deemed disposal</span></div>
        <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-2); margin:0;">
