          you're a temporary resident (see above), in which case it doesn't apply. SouthernCross
          gets its own separate exclusion regardless. Kowhai likely doesn't get that same
          carve-out (it's a NZ scheme, not Australian super) — it'd fall back to ordinary
          treatment. A deferral election is available too: keep treating an asset as taxable
          Australian property until it's actually sold, pushing the tax point out indefinitely.
        </p>
