          taxed on a deemed annual return (5% of opening value, or actual gain — your choice each
          year), not on realised gains. Two exemptions that might sound relevant don't actually
          apply here: the Australian-shares exemption doesn't reach Meridian's holdings (they're
          US-listed, not ASX-listed companies), and the transitional-resident exemption needs
          10+ years overseas — well short of a near-term return.
        </p>
